          "text": "Happy to help\u2014what area are you in, and do you need weekend/24\u2011hour care or CHAS/Healthier SG support? If you want a quick shortlist, these are solid, easy-to-book options:\n\n- 24-hour walk\u2011in GPs: Central 24\u2011HR Clinic Group has multiple 24/7 clinics across the island, useful for late nights and weekends. ([centralclinic.com.sg](https://www.centralclinic.com.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- Raffles Medical (airport branches): The Changi Airport Terminal 3 (B2) and Terminal 4 clinics run 24/7; Raffles Hospital also has a 24\u2011hour acute and critical care centre if you need A&E\u2011level support. ([rafflesmedicalgroup.com](https://www.rafflesmedicalgroup.com/clinic/raffles-medical-terminal-3-clinic/?utm_source=openai))\n- Parkway Shenton: Large, reputable GP chain with 38+ clinics islandwide; supports CHAS and Healthier SG. Example branch info and services here. ([parkwayshenton.com.sg](https://www.parkwayshenton.com.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- HMI OneCare Clinics: Islandwide family GP network with many outlets open evenings and on weekends; see live hours by location. ([onecaremedical.com.sg](https://www.onecaremedical.com.sg/clinics/?utm_source=openai))\n- SATA CommHealth: Non\u2011profit medical centres offering GP consults and basic screenings at generally affordable rates; check the locator for the nearest site. ([sata.com.sg](https://www.sata.com.sg/departments/gp-service/?utm_source=openai))\n\nTell me your neighbourhood (e.g., Bishan, Tampines, Jurong) and any preferences (budget, 24/7, languages, children\u2019s care), and I\u2019ll narrow it to the best nearby clinic and share today\u2019s opening hours."
